# 🌱 ECO-SAVER

ECO-SAVER is a web application built to help users track and reduce their environmental impact. It combines a carbon footprint tracker, eco-habit tracking, community action tools, and an educational library on sustainability topics into a single platform.

## ✨ Features

- **Carbon Footprint Tracker** – log and monitor your daily/monthly carbon footprint (`carbon-footprint-tracker.html`)
- **Eco Habit Tracking** – track sustainable habits over time (`eco-habit-tracking.html`)
- **Dashboard** – a central overview of your eco stats (`dashboard.html`)
- **Community Action** – discover and take part in local environmental initiatives (`community-action.html`)
- **Local Ecological Issues** – view region-specific ecological concerns (`local-ecological-issues.html`)
- **Educational Library & Awareness Hub** – articles and resources on biodiversity, freshwater, and renewable energy (`educational-library.html`, `ecoawarenesshub.html`, `article-*.html`)
- **Interactive Challenges** – gamified eco-challenges to encourage sustainable behavior (`interactive-challenges.html`)
- **Authentication** – login/signup flow with OTP-based verification (`login.html`, `signup.html`, `login.js`, `login.css`)
- **AI Image Support** – AI-powered image features via a dedicated backend service

## 📁 Project Structure

```
ECO-SAVER/
├── ai-image-backend/              # Backend service handling AI image generation/processing
├── otp-backend/                   # Backend service handling OTP generation & verification for auth
├── landing.html                   # Landing page (entry point)
├── login.html / signup.html       # Authentication pages
├── login.js / login.css / save.js # Auth & shared client-side scripts
├── dashboard.html                 # Main user dashboard
├── carbon-footprint-tracker.html  # Carbon footprint tracking tool
├── eco-habit-tracking.html        # Habit tracking tool
├── ecotracker.html                # Eco tracking overview
├── community-action.html          # Community initiatives
├── local-ecological-issues.html   # Local ecological issue reports
├── interactive-challenges.html    # Gamified challenges
├── educational-library.html       # Learning resources
├── ecoawarenesshub.html           # Awareness hub
├── article-biodiversity.html      # Article: biodiversity
├── article-freshwater.html        # Article: freshwater ecosystems
├── article-renewable.html         # Article: renewable energy
├── EcoSaver_SIH_Presentation.*    # Project presentation (SIH)
└── avtar1.png ... avtar5.png      # Avatar/profile images
```

> **Note:** The root currently also contains a few files with generic names (`abc.html`, `new.html`, `card.html`) left over from development. These are being tracked separately for cleanup — see open issues.

## 🚀 Getting Started

### Prerequisites
- [Node.js](https://nodejs.org/) (v16 or higher recommended)
- npm (comes with Node.js)
- A modern web browser

### 1. Clone the repository
```bash
git clone https://github.com/Dipanshu8384/ECO-SAVER.git
cd ECO-SAVER
```

### 2. Run the frontend
The frontend is plain HTML/CSS/JS. You can open `landing.html` directly in your browser, or serve the folder with a simple static server for correct relative paths and API calls:
```bash
npx serve .
# or
python -m http.server 5500
```

### 3. Set up the OTP backend
```bash
cd otp-backend
npm install
```
Create a `.env` file in `otp-backend/` with the required variables (e.g. email/SMS provider credentials, port). Example:
```
PORT=5001
EMAIL_USER=your_email@example.com
EMAIL_PASS=your_app_password
```
Then start the server:
```bash
npm start
```

### 4. Set up the AI image backend
```bash
cd ai-image-backend
npm install
```
Create a `.env` file in `ai-image-backend/` with the required API keys (e.g. your image-generation provider key, port). Example:
```
PORT=5002
AI_API_KEY=your_api_key_here
```
Then start the server:
```bash
npm start
```

> ⚠️ Exact environment variable names may differ — please check each backend folder's source code (`index.js`/`server.js`) for the specific variables it expects, and update this section if they differ.

